  "id": "COMPOUND:31694 - PROTEIN:6020",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Batilol, (R)- may interact with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through a series of target relationships. Specifically, Batilol, (R)- is targeted by Inosine-5'-monophosphate dehydrogenase 1 and E-selectin, which in turn are targeted by Cryptophycin 23. Both Inosine-5'-monophosphate dehydrogenase 1 and Cryptophycin 23 are known to target the same downstream kinase, PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1. This suggests a potential pathway where Batilol, (R)- may influence the activity of CDC2L1 through its interaction with these intermediate targets. The evidence supports a mechanistic link where Batilol, (R)- could act as a modulator of the kinase activity via these intermediate proteins, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
